# NovaDeck installer -- Wi-Fi settings.
#
# HOW TO USE THIS FILE
#   1. Copy it, in this same folder, to a file named exactly:   wifi.conf
#   2. Open the copy and put your network name and password below.
#   3. Eject the card, put it back in the device, and switch it on.
#
# The installer downloads NovaDeck over the network, so it needs a network to join. If you
# would rather not use Wi-Fi at all, plug a USB-C Ethernet adapter into the device instead --
# that needs no file and no editing.
#
# Leave this example file alone so it is still here next time. The installer only reads
# wifi.conf; it ignores this one.
#
# NOTES
#   - Only these two settings are read. Anything else is an error, and the installer will tell
#     you which line it did not understand.
#   - A line starting with # is a comment.
#   - Quotes around the values are optional. Spaces in a network name are fine.
#   - The password is never shown on screen and is never written to the log.
#   - 5 GHz networks are supported.
#
# Replace the two values below.

SSID=my network name
PSK=my wifi password
